   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Sunday, December 4, 2016 at 12:04:01 PM UTC-5, Bruno Nicenboim wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Since\n I moved from stan 2.9 to stan 2.12 together with updating the version \nof Ubuntu I&#39;m getting sefaults quite often (once every ten times I run \nmodels).<br>It happens with different models, most of them pretty \nsimple. Should I open a bug? Or is there some incompatibility with \nsomething from my session?<br></div></blockquote><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You have to install Rcpp with the same compiler (settings). The r-cran-rcpp package may be compiled differently, depending on versions and stuff. Just do<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">install</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Rcpp&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
